    "summary": "Gown (boubou, tobe); composed of a single width of European calico cotton, forming a rectangle. A circular hole has been cut into the centre for the wearer’s head. The cloth has been tie resist-dyed indigo along the weft in such a way to produce four wide bands of striations between five narrower bands of solid indigo. The entire cloth was twice dyed in indigo, once overall, and again after the ties had been removed to form a lighter blue decoration within the four decorative bands.",
